WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:00.900
No differences,

2
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.160
what I would say here again

3
00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.080
is that for the vast majority of people,

4
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.370
this is going to make no difference.

5
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:07.440
Can I say for sure

6
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.960
that with a bodybuilder

7
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.110
who's at very little body fat levels,

8
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.770
that it might not make a difference?

9
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:14.090
No.

10
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.650
I know a colleague of mine, Lyle McDonald,

11
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:18.890
who's a really astute fitness pro,

12
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:23.620
has hypothesized that it might be a good strategy

13
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:25.740
to use when you're very low body fat

14
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.540
to get a couple extra, a pound or so

15
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:29.830
of extra fat loss.

16
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:34.050
I cannot, from what we've done, refute that.

17
00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.700
But for the vast majority, again,

18
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.540
you're talking such a minute amount of people,

19
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:40.620
and the vast majority of people doing cardio

20
00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.850
are not people that are at 6% body fat,

21
00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:45.080
7% body fat,

22
00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:48.530
they're people at 12, 14, 18% body fat,

23
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.030
and it's missing the forest from the trees.

24
00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:54.160
You're doing all that, you're going nuts

25
00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.260
trying to not eat before you do your cardio

26
00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:00.370
when have one less donut,

27
00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.800
and it's going to have a much bigger impact

28
00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:02.650
on your body comp.
